Create one realistic business email thread grounded only in the supplied plan.

Thread plan:
{{ thread_plan | tojson }}

Requirements:
- Return JSON only.
- Return exactly {{ thread_plan.message_count }} messages in chronological order.
- Use only the exact participant email addresses supplied in the plan.
- The first message must follow communication direction {{ thread_plan.communication_direction }}:
  sender type {{ thread_plan.sender_entity_type }} to recipient type(s)
  {{ thread_plan.recipient_entity_types | join(", ") }}.
- Sender role is {{ thread_plan.sender_role or "external contact" }} and sender
  department is {{ thread_plan.sender_department or "external" }}. Relationship:
  {{ thread_plan.relationship }}.
- Employee-to-customer communication must be polished and omit internal-only
  details. Customer-to-employee messages should ask, confirm, dispute, or supply
  information naturally.
- Employee-to-vendor and vendor-to-employee communication should use appropriate
  purchasing, fulfillment, billing, or payment language. Employee-to-employee
  communication may use concise internal terminology.
- Each message must contain sender, to (an array), cc (an array), subject, text, and date.
- Preserve the workflow facts, dates, status, record identifiers, and amounts. Do not invent financial facts.
- Make replies sound natural, concise, and distinct. Do not include signatures; they are added later.
- Reflect tone {{ thread_plan.tone }} and personality {{ thread_plan.mbti }}.
{% if thread_plan.topic %}
- Briefly and naturally mention {{ thread_plan.topic }} in no more than one message.
{% else %}
- Stay directly on the work topic.
{% endif %}
- Dates must be ISO dates no earlier than the workflow date.

Return this shape:
{"emails":[{"sender":"exact address","to":["exact address"],"cc":[],"subject":"...","text":"...","date":"YYYY-MM-DD"}]}
